{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1416359-strange-assembly-s-v5-one-year-later-podcast","id":1416359,"title":"Strange Assembly's \"V5 - One Year Later\" podcast","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-10-01T15:03:08-07:00","id":1416359,"title":"Strange Assembly's \"V5 - One Year Later\" podcast","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.strangeassembly.com/2019/episode-266-v5-one-year-later\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.strangeassembly.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/08/V5-Core-book.jpg?fit=927%2C1200&amp;ssl=1\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.strangeassembly.com/2019/episode-266-v5-one-year-later\" target=\"_blank\"> Episode 266 &ndash; V5 One Year Later </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.strangeassembly.com/2019/episode-266-v5-one-year-later\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.strangeassembly.com/2019/episode-266-v5-one-year-later </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> The latest episode of the Strange Assembly podcast is now available for download! Chris and Craig have some conversation about the nitty-gritty of the fifth edition of Vampire: the Masquerade one y&hellip; </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I really enjoyed this podcast and think it manages to talk about a lot of very intesting rules changes and what works as well as doesn't in V5:<br /> <br /> * The difficulty in V5 is far too punishing and should be lowered by 1 at least or just not that many rolls for difficulty.<br /> <br /> * Hunger checks are way too taxing as are hunting rules.<br /> <br /> * Domain/Chasis is probably the &quot;one background to rule them all&quot;<br /> <br /> * The lessening of vampire weaknesses was a smart move and most of them are just good ideas (Gangrel, Nosferatu, Malkavian)<br /> <br /> * Combing Disciplines and removing &quot;unique&quot; Disciplines was probably a very good idea.<br /> <br /> * Very little talk about metaplot<br /> <br /> I think this is a must-listen for vampire fans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-01T15:19:14-07:00","id":1416362,"title":"","content":"Well, I agree with those points except for the Disciplines and Weaknesses ones ( Possibly with the exception of the Malkavian one); part of the fun of playing a Gangrel and a Nossie are the fact that you end up looking every bit the monster you are.<br /> <br /> Might check it out especially seeing as 25YOVTM has crashed and burned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-01T15:25:08-07:00","id":1416365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1416359-strange-assembly-s-v5-one-year-later-podcast?p=1416362#post1416362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I agree with those points except for the Disciplines and Weaknesses ones ( Possibly with the exception of the Malkavian one); part of the fun of playing a Gangrel and a Nossie are the fact that you end up looking every bit the monster you are.</div> </div> </div> </div>I honestly was kind of treating it that way anyway. The ancient Gangrel like Inyanga, Karsh, and others weren't very monstrous.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Might check it out especially seeing as 25YOVTM has crashed and burned. </div> </div> </div>I dunno, as much as I miss the &quot;Jay and Silent Bob&quot; dynamic, I will say that creating a large panel of guys reviewing the books isn't terrible.<br /> <br /> The timing of it was also not terrible as they're about to finish the entirety of V:TM as a whole.<br /> <br /> So if it had to be a place where it broke up ala TWO BEST FRIENDS PLAY then it wasn't far from completing the entire tabletop line. I understand Werewolf is next.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-02T07:38:33-07:00","id":1416473,"title":"","content":"I really like their POV, and the only thing I didn't agree with, was their take on Hunger.<br /> <br /> Like, it's called Hunger for a reason. If you're hungry, you will want to eat something. Creating a scenario in which you wake up with Hunger 3, and have to deal with it for the rest of the game is just silly to me.<br /> <br /> And I get their reasoning for not wanting to RP Hunting every time [I don't really see a reason to RP it when the players picked their Predator type] because you can just do the Predator Hunting roll and move on. But then again, I don't practice failure in V5. You either succeed or have to face consequences, it lets the story run more smoothly.<br /> <br /> Overall, pretty good talk.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Constantinople was <b>not</b> a mistake.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26438-thedreamapologist","name":"TheDreamApologist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26438_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}